{"name":"Heliotrope Grey","hex":"#ab98a9","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"heliotrope","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A plant with flowers which turn to face and follow the sun, such as  marigolds and sunflowers.","A plant of the genus Heliotropium, especially a common heliotrope (Heliotropium arborescens), which has clusters of purple flowers with a strong fragrance."]},{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Of a light purple or violet colour like that of Heliotropium arborescens flowers."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/heliotrope"},{"term":"grey","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Commonwealth standard spelling of gray.","Synonym of coloured (pertaining to the mixed race of black and white)."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["Commonwealth standard spelling of gray."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/grey"}],"entries":[{"title":"Heliotrope (bloodstone)","blocks":[{"text":"Heliotrope, is a mineral aggregate, a cryptocrystalline mixture of quartz that occurs mostly as jasper (opaque) or sometimes as chalcedony (translucent)."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/87/Quarz_-_Heliotrop_%28Blutjaspis%29.JPG/330px-Quarz_-_Heliotrop_%28Blutjaspis%29.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Heliotrope_(bloodstone)","wikidata":"Q430174"},{"title":"Heliotrope (building)","blocks":[{"text":"The Heliotrope is an environmentally friendly housing project by German architect Rolf Disch. There are three such buildings in Germany. The first experimental version was built in 1994 as the architect's home in Freiburg im Breisgau, while the other two were used as exhibition buildings for the Hansgrohe company in Offenburg and a dentist's lab in Hilpoltstein in Bavaria."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/5f/Heliotrop_Freiburg.jpg/330px-Heliotrop_Freiburg.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Heliotrope_(building)","wikidata":"Q325460"},{"title":"Grey","blocks":[{"text":"Grey or gray is an intermediate color between black and white. It is a neutral or achromatic color, meaning that it has no chroma. It is the color of a rain or storm cloud, of ash, and of lead."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/1e/Loxodonta_africana_by_Ron_Cogswell.jpg/330px-Loxodonta_africana_by_Ron_Cogswell.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Grey","wikidata":"Q42519"},{"title":"Heliotrope (color)","blocks":[{"text":"Heliotrope is a pink-purple tint that is a representation of the colour of the heliotrope flower."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/f2/Heliotropium_peruvianum.jpg/330px-Heliotropium_peruvianum.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Heliotrope_(color)","wikidata":"Q2296108"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/23/Bloodstone_4_%2849036280821%29.jpg/500px-Bloodstone_4_%2849036280821%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/23/Bloodstone_4_%2849036280821%29.jpg/1280px-Bloodstone_4_%2849036280821%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/23/Bloodstone_4_%2849036280821%29.jpg/500px-Bloodstone_4_%2849036280821%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"A rough specimen of bloodstone","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ABloodstone_4_(49036280821).jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/20/Heliotrop_%28Geb%C3%A4ude%29.jpg/500px-Heliotrop_%28Geb%C3%A4ude%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikiped